se they refused to  get a a vaccination should they be  rehired  well i would leave that up to the  individual corporation  our policy and recommendation was to  have an immunization policy uh whether  you vaccinate or uh get tested uh if  they've gone forward and had a mandate  which was not our direction  i would leave it up to the individual  corporation to negotiate that with their  workforce  follow-up and this is the last question  would you doctor feel confident  that  an unvaccinated person  could go and work in a long-term care  facility now  well it's a good question i i think  we've improved the infection prevention  and control practices uh significantly  in long-term care  i think as we head to low endemicity  and low-risk environments in that  setting we should absolutely review  all  measures that have been put in play  but  infection prevention control practices  so masking and hand hygiene  all those  practices that work so well before we  have vaccine have to be  monitored you need good quality  assurance that they're maintained and  the workforce is educated in them  realize their benefit  and i think that's one of the biggest  lessons learned from  our long-term care activities is how to  ensure ongoing sustained  benefit of the baseline infection  prevention control practices to best  protect their clientele  thanks everyone

